version: 2.0.0
description: >-
  `paradigm purpose` subcommands. validate.ts is #purpose-validate-command: it
  validates one .purpose file, or every .purpose under a directory found with
  purpose-core getAllPurposeFiles({ respectGitignore: true }), so gitignored
  build and release output (e.g. packages/gnomon/release/Gnomon.app) is never
  validated as a symbol source; outside a git work tree release/ is skipped by
  name, and dist/, build/, node_modules/ are always skipped (DEFAULT_PURPOSE_IGNORE).
  remember.ts is #purpose-remember-command (aggregate and print purpose context).
  Both symbols are declared in packages/paradigm/.purpose.
context:
  - "Tests: packages/paradigm/tests/purpose-validate-path.test.ts (path shapes, release/gitignore skip)."
